  "question": "The task management module of a genome analysis system is structured as follows: The system includes a task table, task parameter table, task-related organism table, and task-excluded organism table. The task table records detailed information for each task, including Task ID, Task Title, Creation Date, Task Status, End Date, Status Reason, Query Statement, Database, Executable File, Algorithm, Options, and Task Owner. The task parameter table records parameter information for each task, including Parameter ID, Task ID, Parameter Name, and Parameter Value. The task-related organism table records organism information associated with each task, including Organism ID, Task ID, and Organism Name. The task-excluded organism table records organism information excluded for each task, including Organism ID, Task ID, and Organism Name. The system utilizes these tables to manage the creation, execution, and result recording of genome analysis tasks.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0384\n\nCREATE TABLE `task` (\n  `task_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `task_title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `creation_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `task_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `end_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `status_reason` varchar(500) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `query_statement` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `database` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `executable_file` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `algorithm` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `options` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `task_owner` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`task_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `task_parameter` (\n  `parameter_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `task_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `parameter_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `parameter_value` varchar(500) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`parameter_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `task_parameter_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`task_id`) REFERENCES `task` (`task_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `task_related_organism` (\n  `organism_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `task_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `organism_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`organism_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `task_related_organism_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`task_id`) REFERENCES `task` (`task_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `task_excluded_organism` (\n  `organism_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `task_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `organism_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`organism_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `task_excluded_organism_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`task_id`) REFERENCES `task` (`task_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
